body:
After spending hours trying to figure out why I could login with Digest through a browser, but not with an Android app. I think I found a little issue.
Here a quick run down:

method from DigestAuthenticate.php. Added log points to try see what is going on

``` php
public function parseAuthData($digest) {
if (substr($digest, 0, 7) === 'Digest ') {
$digest = substr($digest, 7);
}
$keys = $match = array();
$req = array('nonce' => 1, 'nc' => 1, 'cnonce' => 1, 'qop' => 1, 'username' => 1, 'uri' => 1, 'response' => 1);
preg_match_all('/(\w+)=([\'"]?)([a-zA-Z0-9@=.\/_-]+)\2/', $digest, $match, PREG_SET_ORDER);
foreach ($match as $i) {
CakeLog::info('i implode - ' . implode(', ', $i));
$keys[$i[1]] = $i[3];
CakeLog::info('unset - ' . $req[$i[1]]);
unset($req[$i[1]]);
}

if (empty($req)) {
CakeLog::info('returning keys ' . $keys);
return $keys;
}
CakeLog::info('Not returning keys - ' . implode(',', $req));
return null;
}
```

The following is from a failed attempt to login with Android app:
A log that is done just before the call to this method shows that $digest param passed in equals

2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: Digest - username="admin", realm="192.168.0.2", nonce="53a7f9b83f61b", uri="http://192.168.0.2/pvcollection/sites/pull/HFDH0001.json", response="5894f5d9cd41d012bac09eeb89d2ddf2", qop=auth, nc=00000001, cnonce="b85ff144e496e6e18d1c73020566ea3b", opaque="6f65e91667cf98dd13464deaf2739fde"

As you can see all the required parts are there. Now in the foreach ($match as $i) loop it iterates through the parts and I output them as logs. Here are the results

2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: i implode - username="admin", username, ", admin
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: unset - 1
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: i implode - realm="192.168.0.2", realm, ", 192.168.0.2
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: unset -
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: i implode - nonce="53a7f9b83f61b", nonce, ", 53a7f9b83f61b
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: unset - 1
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: i implode - response="5894f5d9cd41d012bac09eeb89d2ddf2", response, ", 5894f5d9cd41d012bac09eeb89d2ddf2
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: unset - 1
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: i implode - qop=auth, qop, , auth
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: unset - 1
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: i implode - nc=00000001, nc, , 00000001
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: unset - 1
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: i implode - cnonce="b85ff144e496e6e18d1c73020566ea3b", cnonce, ", b85ff144e496e6e18d1c73020566ea3b
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: unset - 1
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: i implode - opaque="6f65e91667cf98dd13464deaf2739fde", opaque, ", 6f65e91667cf98dd13464deaf2739fde
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: unset -
2014-06-23 09:56:08 Debug: Not returning keys - 1

Now as you can see at the bottom is false, and my app never logs in. The missing Item is 'uri'. Now as you can see it is in the original $digest, so I can only assume it is something to do with the preg_match_all functions (which I don't 100% understand)

Now if I do a login with a browser on pc, the login is successful and the only thing that is different (format wise) is the the uri does NOT contain 'http://'. So, I assume the ':' is making the mess in the preg_match_all. 
Not sure if this is a bug in cake or Android. In android, the credentials response is pretty much auto, so I would be a system bug, not something in my code.
